WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/dashboard/components/MiniGridPreview.tsx — a PURE presentational thumbnail of a
  `SavedDashboard` layout. It imports `GRID_COLS` (lg = 4) and `getWidgetDef` (the shared widget registry) and:
    lgLayout = dashboard.layouts.lg ?? []
    cols     = GRID_COLS.lg                                  // 4
    maxY     = lgLayout.length > 0 ? Math.max(...map(y+h)) : 2
    safeMaxY = (maxY > 0 && Number.isFinite(maxY)) ? maxY : 2
    container: relative w-full, aspectRatio cols/safeMaxY, rounded-lg, bg-white/[0.02], border-white/[0.06]
    per item : absolute box at left=x/cols, top=y/safeMaxY, width=w/cols, height=h/safeMaxY (percentages),
               padding 2px, rounded-sm, bg-white/[0.06], border-white/[0.08], centring
               getWidgetDef(widget.widgetId)?.icon (h-3 w-3 text-muted) when the widget+def resolve.
  No data hooks; the prompt records "Data sources: (none)" + "Shared components used: (none)" + "i18n keys:
  (none extracted — surface is anonymous)". So the remote loading/empty/error/stale/offline branches belong to
  the data-bound caller (the dashboard manager), NOT to the preview — the same disposition the sibling
  presentational surfaces HighlightCard (0076) and ToolCard (0010) carry.

